n-of-spying-on-journalists/a-79931583?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A London court has found two Iranian citizens guilty of surveilling reporters for a Persian-language television station critical of Iran's government. One was also convicted of planning a violent attack against them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Impeachment: How it works and why Trump should be worried</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3560b76a5279519cb3bf8c7ec89237ddb01abfecd0faf7250c92f5e0bcae90fb</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/impeachment-how-it-works-and-why-trump-should-be-worried/a-79931040--faa8753db476.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/impeachment-how-it-works-and-why-trump-should-be-worried/a-79931040?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pete Hegseth, Bill Clinton and Donald Trump (twice so far): attempts to impeach political figures are becoming common. The failure rate looks high, but according to experts, conviction is not always the aim.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang: Spy row, second affair leaves Nvidia without its rockstar CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:354f94f00f9901f54cc5b85d9793b049c813628d8ba82335b231159e1e79937e</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-second-affair-leaves-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972--471686cc8872.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-second-affair-leaves-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang, who built Nvidia into the world’s dominant AI chipmaker, is stepping down as CEO after a second affair came to light. DW examines how losing its figurehead w